IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wra-core`

-- wra-definitions.l4: the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (United Kingdom), 2012 c. 5, definitions that fall in the keel's range.
-- There are none. The keel's range is line 1 of inputs/ukpga-2012-5.txt, the enacting formula
-- ("Be it enacted by the Queen's most Excellent Majesty ... as follows:"), which defines no term (inert, reason 1: not operative).
-- Every definition of the Act is in a part's range, so each part encodes its own as a defined-term function over the core:
-- PLAN.md section 9 lists them by part and raw line (wra1: s 40 and the definitions it points to; wra2: the interpretation
-- text the ESA and JSA sections insert; wra3: s 95; wra4: s 96(10)).
-- This file defines nothing and tests nothing; it exists so that the name the merge checklist uses resolves, and it is the
-- place the lead may put a definition hoisted out of two parts at the merge.
-- The file the keel does test is wra-core-tests.l4 (every type in wra-core.l4 can be built and read back).
